{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-224226","model_call":17,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"guns in public places\" \"guns in public\" \"public carry\") (+ ban banned prohibit restrict) (+ \"public safety\" violence intimidation shootings))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"guns in public places\" \"guns in public\" \"public carry\") (+ ban banned prohibit restrict) (+ \"public safety\" violence intimidation shootings))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_441934189#0_1203957524","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3686","rank":1,"snippet":"Panthers Carried Guns, Conservatives Supported Gun Control reader When Black Panthers Carried Guns, Conservatives Supported Gun Control The debate around guns has not always been the partisan stalemate it is today. But it has, like so many other political issues in the US, always been partly about race. By Joshua Manson Joshua Manson BuzzFeed Contributor Posted on August 9, 2019, at 11:14 a.m. ET Bettmann / Bettmann Archive A Black Panther Party member holds a rifle outside the California State Capitol on May 2, 1967, during a protest against a bill that <cover>banned carrying loaded guns in public. The images from the two mass shootings </cover>this past weekend — in El Paso, Texas, and Dayton, Ohio — were, as with all mass shootings, devastating. No matter how many news cycles come and go, it is impossible to stay numb to the story of a woman in El Paso who was shielding her baby son so that her dead body’s fall broke his bones while saving his life. But for the generation that came of age in the wake of the 1999 Columbine shooting, these horrors and the constant anxiety that they bring have begun to feel normal — even inevitable. There "},"time":869},"model_calls":17,"document_judgments":15,"relevance_3":5,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
